  <x:String x:Key="logs.empty">No warnings or errors.</x:String>

  <!-- NurCRM support -->
  <x:String x:Key="remoteSupport.intro">Remote help uses AnyDesk. Click the button below — AnyDesk will open with a connection address (ID). Read that address to the support agent over the phone or WhatsApp.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="remoteSupport.launchButton">Launch AnyDesk</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="remoteSupport.downloadButton">Download AnyDesk</x:String>

  <!-- Knowledge base -->
  <x:String x:Key="kb.subtitle">Answers to common questions about running the till. Click a question to see the answer.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="kb.catFeaturesTitle">App features</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.offlineQ">Can I work without internet?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.offlineA">Yes. The till keeps ringing up sales offline — they're saved locally and sent to the server automatically as soon as the connection comes back. The number of receipts waiting to send is shown in the status bar at the bottom of the screen.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.deferredCartsQ">What are "Held carts"?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.deferredCartsA">Lets you hold the current receipt (for example, if the customer went to get money) and come back to it later without losing the items in the cart. Opens from the side menu.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.themesQ">Can I change how the till looks?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.themesA">Yes — in "Marketplace" → "Themes" you can pick a ready-made look or set your own accent color, font and corner rounding. Some themes are paid — 2 are free (Gold, Blue), the rest unlock with a serial number.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.zeroStockQ">What if a product is out of stock but the customer wants to buy it?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.zeroStockA">When adding a product with zero stock, the till will show a warning and ask you to confirm the sale — once confirmed, enter how much to add to stock. Stock updates automatically and the sale goes through as usual.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.irregularReceiptsQ">What are "Irregular receipts"?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.irregularReceiptsA">A section in the side menu that automatically collects receipts that went through in a non-standard way: sold at zero stock, server-upload errors, receipts still uploading. Useful for reconciling at the end of a shift.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="kb.catCashierTitle">How the cashier role works and what's available</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.permissionsQ">What permissions can a cashier be given?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.permissionsA">Permissions are granted per employee in NurCRM (the web panel): access to till settings, scales, price tags, discounts, price changes, removing items from the cart, warehouse/purchasing, suppliers, returns, sales (reports), and shifts. Sections without a granted permission are hidden or unavailable in the till menu.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.financeAccessQ">Why can't the cashier see "Finance" or "Sales"?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.financeAccessA">These sections are only open to employees with the matching permission ("Sales", etc.) granted in NurCRM. If a section is missing, that permission hasn't been granted to this employee.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.shiftQ">How do I open/close a shift?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.shiftA">The "Open shift"/"Close shift" buttons are on the top bar of the till. Open a shift before the first sale of the day and close it at the end — closing shows a report of revenue and the cash balance.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="kb.catUpdatesTitle">How to update the app</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.checkUpdateQ">How do I know if there's a new version of the till?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.checkUpdateA">The till checks for updates on every launch by itself. You can check manually in Settings → Updates → "Check for updates" — the "Update" button appears there too if a new version is found.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.rollbackQ">Can I roll back to an earlier version if something breaks after an update?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.rollbackA">Yes — Settings → Updates has a list of previous versions you can roll back to.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="kb.catFailureTitle">What to do if something goes wrong, and who to contact</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.errorDialogQ">The till showed an error window — what do I do?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.errorDialogA">The error window has 2 buttons: "Close" — just closes the window, and "Defer error" — the error gets logged (in "Logs and errors") and work continues as if nothing happened. Use "Defer error" when the error doesn't stop you from continuing to work right now.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.logsQ">Where can I see what happened during a failure?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.logsA">Side menu → "Logs and errors" — shows recent warnings, errors and server disconnects. The "Open logs folder" button opens the folder with detailed technical files — you can send these to support.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.remoteSupportQ">How do I get remote help from NurCRM support?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.remoteSupportA">Side menu → "NurCRM support" → "Launch AnyDesk". A connection address (ID) will appear — read it to the support agent by phone or WhatsApp so they can connect to your computer and help.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.printerQ">The till doesn't see a receipt printer connected over USB — what do I do?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.printerA">In Settings → Printing, click "Find" again (the list doesn't refresh on its own). If the printer was set up via Zadig and still doesn't show up — reconnect it and try again, or contact support via "NurCRM support".</x:String>
